  "task": {
    "objective": "Deliver at least two milk portions from each of three herd owners to the shared barn before a herd loses all health; maintain grazing access, water and repairable gates.",
    "natural_termination": "Failure when any herd health reaches zero. Otherwise success when every owner's delivered count is at least two. Failure excludes simultaneous success; either natural cause takes priority over the cap.",
    "interaction": "Opening or repairing a gate changes another owner's herd route, grazing pressure and future milk. Shared trough water, regrowth neighborhoods, one bucket, one hammer and single-slot carrying make irrigation, repair, collection and delivery compete for the same workers.",
    "observation_access": "Fully observable. Every role receives its one-hot and all public obs_keys leaves: actual map, shepherds and their cargo, herd coordinates/owners/needs/health/milk, gate condition/open state, grass and rest, trough water, tool locations/holders/charges, facilities, boards and delivery/production events. Herd, tool and scene information is the same for humans and policies. No hidden animal target or private planner is exposed through rendering; target selection is recomputed directly from visible native state."
